        <mxCell id="aNL9TuHRUiQOc67SNU_S-7" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Add some logic to decide if the process has both top and bottom halo information.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Each process should ONLY store the data it&#39;s responsible for plus the halo information. The vector should be appropriately sized according to what the process needs.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;When reading, each process will use read_at(offset, vector.data(), layout). The offset will be the header size + all of u + any v data before halo.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&quot;H&quot; is the diagram will be filled with actual values. Left as &quot;H&quot; to help clearly distinguish when it&#39;s needed.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
